    {
      "text": "June 28, 2022 agenda report: the project demolishes six commercial buildings and one single-family residence and builds a four-story, 50-unit condominium building with two levels of underground parking (113 spaces), 34 interior bicycle spaces and a private rooftop area. The draft resolution grants a 35% density bonus and one incentive allowing a 46-foot height where 35 feet applies, plus a waiver for a 17.5-foot elevator overrun.",
      "src": [
        "SRC-003468",
        "SRC-003469"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Affordable units: the agenda report's Table 2 lists 7 BMR units (1 very low-income studio, 3 one-bedrooms with 2 very low-income and 1 moderate, and 3 moderate two-bedrooms). The draft resolution findings list three very low-income and four moderate units, and its recitals list one very low-income, two low-income and four moderate units. The state report shows 3 very low-income and 4 moderate.",
      "src": [
        "SRC-003468",
